**Hypothesis**

```prolog
%  A train is eastbound iff one of the three alternatives holds
%   (a) it has a car numbered 4 whose wall is full and the train also
%       contains a *different* car that carries exactly one payload item;
%   (b) it has a car whose wall is full, payload is a golden vase and the
%       load consists of exactly two items;
%   (c) it has a car whose wall is full, payload is a diamond, the load
%       consists of exactly one item and the car is **not** the 4‑th car.
eastbound(T) :-
    (   has_car(T,C4), car_num(C4,4), has_wall(C4,full),
        has_car(T,CL), load_num(CL,1), C4 \= CL
    )
    ;
    (   has_car(T,G), has_payload(G,golden_vase), has_wall(G,full),
        load_num(G,2)
    )
    ;
    (   has_car(T,D), has_payload(D,diamond), load_num(D,1),
        has_wall(D,full), car_num(D,N), N \= 4
    ).
```

